s of about 100 K s-1 ).","second_reader_agrees":false,"synthesis":"arc melting with a non-consumable tungsten electrode on a water-cooled copper hearth under purified Ar (cooling rates of about 100 K s-1 )","type":"sample"},{"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-GO545ICUJR","label":"samples nos. 2, 3, 7 and 11","page":6,"quote":"The solidus temperature for the samples nos. 2, 3, 7 and 11 (incipient melting) were also determined using the method devised by Pirani and Alterthum [31].","second_reader_agrees":true,"type":"sample"},{"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-BS4JKAW5BM","label":"no. 18 in Table 2","measured_composition":"Ti25.3 Nb19.0 Al55.7","page":7,"quote":"Within the frame of the present work the standard enthalpy of formation at 298 K was experimentally determined for the ␥ single-phase sample Ti25.3 Nb19.0 Al55.7 (no. 18 in Table 2) annealed for 8 h at 1673 K.","second_reader_agrees":true,"type":"sample"},{"extraction_accepted":false,"id":"ORC-QEDDB2A5TZ","nominal_composition":"nominal Nb content of 8 at.% and Al contents of 45, 46, 47 and 48 at.%, respectively","page":7,"quote":"Fig. 6 depicts selected heating curves obtained by DTA for a series of samples with the nominal Nb content of 8 at.% and Al contents of 45, 46, 47 and 48 at.%, respectively.","second_reader_agrees":false,"type":"sample"},{"applies_to":"Ti25.3 Nb19.0 Al55.7 (no. 18 in Table 2)","duration":"8 h","duration_parsed":{"hours":8.0,"printed":"8 h"},"extraction_accepted":true,"id":"ORC-T3AE2O3YMS","page":7,"quote":"Within the frame of the present work the standard enthalpy of formation at 298 K was experimentally determined for the ␥ single-phase sample Ti25.3 Nb19.0 Al55.7 (no. 18 in Table 2) annealed for 8 h at 1673 K.","second_reader_agrees":true,"temperature":{"T_K":1673.0,"converted_in_code":false,"printed":"1673 K","unit_basis":"printed_with_value","unit_printed":"K","value_printed":1673.0},"temperature_printed":"1673 K","temperature_status":"parsed_from_printed","type":"treatment"}